  "summary": "On 25 April 1974 left-leaning Portuguese military officers, the Armed Forces Movement, overthrew the authoritarian Estado Novo government in a coup centred on Lisbon. Civilians joined the soldiers in the streets. The coup opened Portugal's democratic transition and the path to ending the colonial war and recognising independence for its African colonies in 1974–1975.",
